et done, but 4.5 is in feature freeze right now so changes have to be pretty concise and necessary.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3032714932/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3034152757","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107767#issuecomment-3034152757","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107767","id":3034152757,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc602X81","user":{"login":"bencmckenna","id":47491782,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NDkxNzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47491782?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bencmckenna","html_url":"https://github.com/bencmckenna","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bencmckenna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bencmckenna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bencmckenna/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bencmckenna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bencmckenna/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bencmckenna/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bencmckenna/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bencmckenna/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bencmckenna/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-04T01:33:00Z","updated_at":"2025-07-04T01:33:00Z","body":"@apples I have a character model with separate head, eyeball and iris meshes. The eyeball should be clipped by the head, and the iris should be clipped by both the eyeball and the head.\r\n\r\n**Head - Write Always 2\r\nEyeball - Read Less than 1\r\nIris - Read Equal 1**\r\n![b](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/edbff16b-f792-4a08-a851-fef3a37040b6)\r\n(Eyeball correctly clipped, but iris invisible)\r\n\r\n**Head - Write Always 2\r\nEyeball - Write Less 1\r\nIris - Read Equal 1**\r\n![c](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/adf3ff40-21c1-4603-bcdb-08250e880048)\r\n(Iris correctly clipped, but eyeballs incorrectly clipped)\r\n\r\n**Head - Write Always 2\r\nEyeball - Read & Write Less than 1\r\nIris - Read Equal 1**\r\n![d](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b422504d-e36c-4a07-b653-02207dbda226)\r\n(Correct clipping!)\r\n\r\nFor the last result I had to convert to a ShaderMaterial so I could set both read and write modes. I'll admit it's a very minor inconvenience, so thanks for taking the time to look into it.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3034152757/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":3},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]